  "notes": "Vwanji is a Bantu language of Tanzania. The 7-vowel system is represented with ɨ and ʉ for /ɪ/ and /ʊ/. Digraphs like mh and nh represent voiceless nasals. The apostrophe is used in ngʼ for /ŋ/ and occasionally as a morpheme boundary or glottal stop (e.g., mʼb).",
